questions.workedExample:
Track the kept set (root = max):

```
5: push        {5}
1: push        {1, 5}  root 5
9: 9 < 5? no   ignore
3: 3 < 5? yes  replace -> {1, 3}
7: 7 < 3? no   ignore
2: 2 < 3? yes  replace -> {1, 2}
```

Result `[1, 2]`, with 2 calls to `heapreplace`. Each replacement costs O(log k); each rejection costs one comparison.

Insert x into lo if x ≤ lo's max, otherwise into hi; then rebalance.

```
5:  lo{5}        hi{}
15: lo{5}        hi{15}
1:  lo{1,5}      hi{15}
3:  lo{1,3,5} -> too big, move 5
    lo{1,3}      hi{5,15}
8:  8 > 3: hi{5,8,15} -> move 5
    lo{1,3,5}    hi{8,15}
```

Median = root of lo = 5. Each insertion is O(log n) and reading the median is O(1).
